1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,583
I planted a seedling and wanted it to
grow immediately.

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:07,973
Grandma: Slowly, slowly, the egg walks
on its own feet.

3
00:00:08,473 --> 00:00:13,799
Just as we were about to go on a picnic,
it rained and spoiled our plans.

4
00:00:14,149 --> 00:00:16,258
Grandma: Everything happens for the
best.

5
00:00:16,758 --> 00:00:22,143
I saw them test the gold in the fire and
asked why they did it.

6
00:00:22,493 --> 00:00:24,827
Grandma: Gold is tested by fire.

7
00:00:25,327 --> 00:00:28,780
The road was long, but we kept going one
step at a time.

8
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,059
Grandma: Whoever keeps going, arrives.

9
00:00:31,559 --> 00:00:35,350
I practised for a long time to learn
this, but at first it was very difficult.

10
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,027
Grandma: Patience is bitter, but its
fruit is sweet.

11
00:00:40,527 --> 00:00:44,535
I fell while learning to ride a bicycle,
but I got up and tried again.

12
00:00:44,885 --> 00:00:47,476
Grandma: One who falls gets up and keeps
going.

13
00:00:47,976 --> 00:00:52,214
When people started gossiping about our
neighbour, I was about to join in.

14
00:00:52,564 --> 00:00:57,975
Grandma: Silence is golden.

15
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:03,501
Our neighbour had no food, and although
we had only a little, we shared it.

16
00:01:03,851 --> 00:01:05,822
Grandma: One who shares never lacks.

17
00:01:06,322 --> 00:01:10,104
My grandmother started making coffee and
the smell filled the house.

18
00:01:10,454 --> 00:01:12,913
Grandma: Coffee is a blessing for the
home.

19
00:01:13,413 --> 00:01:18,885
Everyone gathered and laughter filled the
house. She has a proverb for this too.

20
00:01:19,235 --> 00:01:22,498
Grandma: When spiderwebs unite, they can
tie up a lion.
